  "changed_since_previous": "Added a fix in BroadcastTransaction to use the mempool's transaction pointer rather than the caller's transaction when rebroadcasting, preventing an unvalidated oversized witness variant from entering the private broadcast queue, along with an updated functional test.",
  "card": "Enforces 12-byte type and 4 MB payload bounds on outbound messages in CConnman::PushMessage(), dropping oversized messages in release builds and asserting in debug builds. Oversized types previously aborted V1 transport or caused buffer overreads/truncation in V2, while callers could bypass payload limits via private rebroadcast of transactions already in the mempool. The sendmsgtopeer RPC now explicitly rejects payloads over 4 MB with an RPC error, and rebroadcasts now use validated mempool transaction instances. It has no dependencies.",
